  "caption": "A long queue left Quinn's back unconvinced, and an old X-ray mentioned a curve. The plan: straighten it by Friday.\n\nKay was honest and kind: in adults, scoliosis care is about pain, endurance and how you move. Curve size often doesn't match symptoms, and exercise is the first step — it can help comfort and function, though it won't straighten an adult curve.\n\nWhat can help: trunk and hip strength plus general fitness, gentle mobility into the directions that feel restricted, pacing standing and walking with short breaks, scoliosis-specific exercise where available, and a chat with your GP about managing pain.\n\nGet it checked if leg symptoms keep progressing, there's weakness, a bladder or bowel change, or the curve looks noticeably worse.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
